[1;33m[2026-03-03 01:38:18,719 [31mINFO [32magents/221-MainProcess[1;33m] [0mObservation: # Campaign Health Assessment & Optimization System\n\n## Executive Summary\nThis analysis evaluates Google Ads campaigns with monthly cost > $1,000 and ROAS < 0.8, identified as high-cost, low-return campaigns. We developed a three-dimensional health score model (Cost Efficiency 40%, Conversion Quality 35%, Competitiveness 25%) to assess 155 campaign-month records from Feb 2023 to Jun 2024.\n\n**Key findings:**\n- 4 campaigns are at **Critical** risk, 75 at **High** risk.\n- 79 (51.0%) of campaigns have health scores below 50 (poor performance).\n- **Search** campaigns perform best (avg health score 69.5), while **Display** campaigns are the worst (avg health score 38.2).\n- **Maximize Conversions** bidding strategy yields the highest health score (65.5); Enhanced CPC is the lowest (35.0).\n- **Finance** industry campaigns show the strongest health (73.7); **Education** campaigns are the weakest (32.0).\n- Geographic distribution: **Canada** delivers the highest ROI (6.36), while **Japan** has the lowest ROI (5.76) among high‑cost campaigns.\n- Device performance: **Tablet** traffic achieves the highest ROI (6.91), slightly ahead of Desktop and Mobile.\n- Trend analysis shows the largest month‑over‑month cost increase occurred in March 2023 (74.9%).\n- Seasonal patterns indicate advertising costs peak in **Month 1** (average $447,563), while conversions are highest in **Month 1**.\n\n## Methodology\n1. **Screening criteria**: Monthly cost > $1,000 and ROAS < 0.8.\n2. **Health Score Model**:\n   - *Cost Efficiency (40%)*: ROAS (higher better) and cost‑per‑conversion (lower better), each normalized to percentile rank.\n   - *Conversion Quality (35%)*: Conversion rate and quality score, normalized.\n   - *Competitiveness (25%)*: Impression share and CTR, normalized.\n3. **Risk levels**: Critical (<25), High (25‑49), Medium (50‑74), Low (≥75).\n4. **Trend analysis**: Month‑over‑month and year‑over‑year growth rates, seasonal averages.\n\n## Campaign Health Assessment Results\n- **Health score distribution**: 7 Low, 69 Medium, 75 High, 4 Critical.\n- **Overall average health score**: 50.2.\n- **Highest‑risk campaigns** (Critical/High) are predominantly in **Display** and **Video** campaign types, using **Enhanced CPC** or **Manual CPC** bidding, in the **Education** and **Real Estate** industries.\n\n## Dimensional Analysis & Risk Factors\n\n### Campaign Type\n| Type | Monthly Records | Total Cost | Avg ROAS | Avg Health Score |\n|------|----------------|------------|----------|------------------|\n| Search | 33 | $1,675,294 | 0.60 | 69.5 |\n| Performance Max | 28 | $1,134,898 | 0.48 | 53.1 |\n| Video | 48 | $1,730,063 | 0.52 | 46.8 |\n| Display | 46 | $2,138,042 | 0.51 | 38.2 |\n\n**Insight**: Search campaigns deliver the best balance of efficiency and conversion quality; Display campaigns suffer from low competitiveness and poor conversion rates.\n\n### Bidding Strategy\n| Strategy | Monthly Records | Total Cost | Avg ROAS | Avg Health Score |\n|----------|----------------|------------|----------|------------------|\n| Maximize Conversions | 17 | $875,023 | 0.52 | 65.5 |\n| Target CPA | 45 | $1,992,947 | 0.60 | 53.7 |\n| Target ROAS | 44 | $1,748,439 | 0.42 | 48.1 |\n| Manual CPC | 32 | $1,348,612 | 0.62 | 47.9 |\n| Enhanced CPC | 17 | $713,277 | 0.43 | 35.0 |\n\n**Insight**: Automated bidding (Maximize Conversions, Target CPA) outperforms manual strategies. Enhanced CPC shows the weakest health, indicating misaligned cost control.\n\n### Industry\n| Industry | Monthly Records | Total Cost | Avg ROAS | Avg Health Score |\n|----------|----------------|------------|----------|------------------|\n| Finance | 16 | $800,271 | 0.69 | 73.7 |\n| Healthcare | 17 | $875,023 | 0.52 | 65.5 |\n| Fashion | 13 | $597,716 | 0.50 | 51.2 |\n| E-commerce | 14 | $765,109 | 0.69 | 48.6 |\n| SaaS | 17 | $566,740 | 0.56 | 47.8 |\n| Travel | 47 | $1,800,242 | 0.52 | 47.2 |\n| Real Estate | 16 | $613,540 | 0.31 | 39.5 |\n| Education | 15 | $659,656 | 0.43 | 32.0 |\n\n**Insight**: Finance and Healthcare campaigns have relatively strong health scores; Education and Real Estate are the most problematic.\n\n### Geographic Distribution\nTop 5 geo targets by cost:\n| Geo Target | Total Cost | ROI | Conversion Rate | Impression Share |\n|------------|------------|-----|----------------|------------------|\n| Japan | $1,051,737 | 5.76 | 1.91% | 40.6% |\n| Australia | $774,453 | 6.19 | 2.22% | 35.4% |\n| United States | $765,000 | 5.87 | 1.70% | 38.5% |\n| United Kingdom | $615,416 | 6.03 | 1.63% | 39.4% |\n| France | $530,705 | 5.97 | 1.72% | 43.1% |\n\n**Insight**: Japan and Australia account for the largest spend, but Japan’s ROI is notably lower. Opportunities exist to shift budget to higher‑ROI regions like Australia and the United States.\n\n### Device Type\n| Device | Total Cost | ROI | Conversion Rate | Impression Share |\n|--------|------------|-----|----------------|------------------|\n| Mobile | $3,971,218 | 6.24 | 1.83% | 39.4% |\n| Desktop | $1,940,088 | 6.33 | 1.79% | 39.2% |\n| Tablet | $658,818 | 6.91 | 1.90% | 39.3% |\n\n**Insight**: Tablet traffic delivers the highest ROI and conversion rate, yet receives the smallest budget allocation. Mobile spends the most but underperforms on ROI.\n\n## Trend Analysis & Seasonality\n- **Month‑over‑month cost growth** peaked at 74.9% in March 2023.\n- **Year‑over‑year cost growth** averaged 75.2% in comparable months.\n- **Seasonal cost peaks** occur in Month 1 (average $447,563), while conversions peak in Month 1.\n- **ROAS trends**: Monthly ROAS fluctuates between 5.01 and 10.17, with no clear long‑term improvement.\n\n## High‑Risk Campaigns Diagnosis\nWe identified 29 campaigns that combine **high cost** and **low conversion rates**. The top 10 by spend are:\n\n| Campaign ID | Month | Cost | Conversions | ROAS | Core Diagnosis |\n|-------------|-------|------|-------------|------|----------------|\n| 36 | 2024-05-01 | $60,725 | 464 | 0.69 | nan |\n| 36 | 2024-02-01 | $60,296 | 740 | 0.69 | nan |\n| 36 | 2024-06-01 | $59,663 | 897 | 0.69 | nan |\n| 36 | 2024-03-01 | $59,148 | 459 | 0.69 | nan |\n| 36 | 2023-05-01 | $58,997 | 474 | 0.69 | nan |\n| 36 | 2023-11-01 | $57,594 | 759 | 0.69 | nan |\n| 36 | 2024-01-01 | $56,576 | 659 | 0.69 | nan |\n| 36 | 2023-12-01 | $53,827 | 642 | 0.69 | nan |\n| 135 | 2024-02-01 | $51,019 | 453 | 0.43 | nan |\n| 36 | 2023-10-01 | $49,550 | 395 | 0.69 | nan |\n\n**Common issues**: Low impression share, poor quality scores, and inefficient CPC contribute to weak competitiveness and conversion quality.\n\n## Optimization Recommendations\n\n### 1. Budget Reallocation\n- Shift spend from **Display** and **Video** campaigns to **Search** campaigns, especially in Finance and Healthcare industries.\n- Reduce budgets for **Enhanced CPC** and **Manual CPC** campaigns; increase budgets for **Maximize Conversions** and **Target CPA**.\n- Reallocate geo spend from **Japan** (lower ROI) to **Australia**, **United States**, and **United Kingdom**.\n- Increase investment in **Tablet** traffic; review mobile‑specific ad creatives and landing pages.\n\n### 2. Keyword Optimization\n- For campaigns with low quality scores (<5), review keyword relevance and ad‑copy alignment.\n- Pause underperforming keywords with high CPC and low conversion rates; expand high‑CTR, high‑conversion‑rate keywords.\n- Use negative keywords to filter irrelevant traffic, especially in Display campaigns.\n\n### 3. Geographic Adjustments\n- Implement geo‑bid adjustments: +20% for Australia and United States; –15% for Japan.\n- Create geo‑specific ad copies for high‑potential regions to improve local relevance.\n\n### 4. Device Bidding Strategies\n- Increase device bid adjustments for tablets by +10‑15%.\n- For mobile campaigns, improve landing‑page mobile experience and load speed to boost conversion rates.\n- Consider device‑specific ad extensions (e.g., click‑to‑call for mobile).\n\n### 5. Campaign‑Level Actions\n- **Critical‑risk campaigns** should undergo immediate auditing: pause, restructure ad groups, refine targeting, and test new creatives.\n- **High‑risk campaigns** can be optimized by improving quality scores through better ad relevance and landing‑page experience.\n- **Medium‑risk campaigns** benefit from incremental bid adjustments and A/B testing of ad copies.\n\n## Conclusion\nBy applying the three‑dimensional health score model, we have pinpointed the root causes of underperformance across campaign types, bidding strategies, industries, geographies, and devices. The recommended actions—budget reallocation, keyword optimization, geographic adjustments, and device‑specific bidding—provide a clear roadmap to improve ROAS and reduce wasteful spend. Continuous monitoring of health scores and seasonal trends will enable proactive campaign management.
